# width: 120
# The pointer over an open menu (src/app/dispatch.zig `menuHover`):
# a mouse-opened File menu (click 12 0 — the dropdown at x 10, its
# rows from y 2) shows no highlight until a row is hovered; the
# hovered row lights with Rust's `▸ ` marker; the pointer on another
# word of the bar switches to that menu (Edit, the brand, the ») —
# Rust's `MenuOpenState::new_mouse(hovered_idx)`; Esc closes. Each
# row ends in its chord (`Ctrl+N`), one cell short of the border.
click 12 0
expect screen contains "│  󰈤  New file                  Ctrl+N │"
expect screen lacks "│▸ 󰈤  New file                  Ctrl+N │"
hover 20 2
expect screen contains "│▸ 󰈤  New file                  Ctrl+N │"
hover 20 3
expect screen contains "│▸   Open file…                Ctrl+P │"
expect screen lacks "│▸ 󰈤  New file                  Ctrl+N │"
hover 18 0
expect screen contains "Find in files…"
expect screen lacks "New file"
hover 3 0
expect screen contains "About mnml…"
expect screen lacks "Find in files…"
hover 23 0
expect screen contains "Selection"
expect screen contains "Terminal"
hover 60 20
expect screen contains "Selection"
key esc
expect screen lacks "Selection"
